\"timedelta(minutes=5)\"'","The grep asserts absence of the old literal but not presence of the shared-constant reference at both sites"],"finding":"AC3's only proving command (grep for the absent `timedelta(minutes=5)` literal) does not prove the AC's positive claim that both the commit and CI repair call sites READ the shared `_COMMIT_TIMEOUT` constant — a site could hardcode `timedelta(minutes=15)` and still pass the grep.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f85a1673f1f0532aa","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, third bullet","norm_id":"n6c730d2143f5a4f3","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer removes the 5-min literal at both sites but wires only one site to _COMMIT_TIMEOUT and inlines timedelta(minutes=15) at the other — grep is green, AC intent unmet"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Augment AC3 with: `grep -n \"_COMMIT_TIMEOUT\" services/orchestration/temporal_workflows/draft_pull_request.py` shows a reference at both the commit and CI-repair activity option sites, and the unit test asserts both start_to_close_timeout values equal _COMMIT_TIMEOUT.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Decide whether to add a subprocess-level timeout to `_git` (or explicitly scope it out with rationale), since the plan documents the no-timeout subprocess as the cause of orphaned clones surviving activity cancellation.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0611,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Evidence: \"`_git` at git_host.py:84 runs subprocess with no timeout, so the thread outlives the activity and the clone keeps running after Temporal has given up.\"","Approach bounds only the Temporal activity budget (5->15 min) and transfer size, not the subprocess: \"cuts exposure roughly fourfold but does not bound the tail\""],"finding":"The plan identifies that `_git` at git_host.py:84 runs subprocess with no timeout so the clone thread outlives the cancelled activity, but the Approach and Acceptance Criteria only raise the activity budget and shrink the transfer — neither bounds the subprocess itself, leaving the orphaned-process failure mode the evidence names unaddressed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb43761b431e11c3b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Evidence section","norm_id":"n9f1e3280d7b54501","priority":0.8889,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A clone still exceeds the 15-minute budget; the worker thread continues running the git subprocess after Temporal cancels the activity, leaking a process and holding resources"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the clone `--branch` target is chosen in each case (existing branch vs. clone base for the create path) and confirm the on-demand blob fetch during `checkout -b <branch> origin/<base>` does not re-expose the transfer tail the blobless clone is meant to bound (e.g. note the checkout fetches only the tree at the resolved ref, not full history).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.064,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["git_host.py:127-132 shows the branch-or-base fallback: `if await self._ls_remote(remote, request.branch): checkout <branch> else: checkout -b <branch> origin/{base}`","A blob:none clone defers blob transfer to checkout; `checkout -b <branch> origin/<base>` materializes the full working tree and will fetch those blobs on demand","Plan quote treats on-demand fetch as free: 'Blobs for the checkout are fetched on demand by the working tree materialisation' — no bound stated"],"finding":"The plan's clone spec `--filter=blob:none --single-branch --branch <branch-or-base>` under-specifies the two-case ref resolution and its interaction with the existing not-yet-created-branch checkout path. commit_and_push has two branches: when request.branch exists it checks it out; when it does not, it runs `checkout -b <branch> origin/<base>` (git_host.py:130-132), which requires the `origin/<base>` remote-tracking ref and materializes the working tree. With a blob:none single-branch clone of `base`, that checkout triggers on-demand blob fetch of the full tree — potentially re-exposing the same transfer tail the plan is trying to bound. The plan asserts on-demand fetch is benign without reasoning about this.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fca333deb873fe9af","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'clone with --filter=blob:none --single-branch --branch <branch-or-base>' and 'Blobs for the checkout are fetched on demand by the working tree materialisation'","norm_id":"n8b72321652001042","priority":0.536,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["First commit onto a branch that does not yet exist on the remote (the not-yet-created path), against the large single-pack repository from the evidence"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocki